-- title:
--   Original top-cap strict clock full cash epsilon bound in signed payment-residual form
-- statement:
--   For the genuine original spectrally negative Levy path, top capital cap, strict pre-ruin clock, and any admissible dividend strategy, the original discounted full payment cash plus initial right-atom w drop and physical-grid signed postpayment w-difference is eventually at most any positive epsilon. Follows from the Proved all-cap cap-linear discounted Stieltjes bound after setting V=w, and the Proved exact original signed-residual sum rearrangement. This supplies the top-cap strict branch of the infinite activity payment-only cash limit with no finite-activity assumptions.

